On Sat, Feb 22, 2003 at 11:44:31AM -0800, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> > No, I don't think you can.  A tanru can only be made out of a
> > combination of brivla, and a pro-sumti represents a sumti, not a
> > brivla (to my mind, an instanciation, a noun, instead of a
> > relationship).

It's easy to put a pronoun in a tanru: you use {me}, which turns a sumti
into a brivla. {do me mi cinmo}.  Or {le xagji me mi cu klama le jubme}.

> Technically incorrect:
> 
> do mi zei cinmo
> 
> "You feel like me."  Sort of.

No, that's a lujvo. If you (for some reason) wanted to make a lujvo out
of that, you could just as easily use the -mib- rafsi.
